{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And as for me, when I came from Paddan.</b> I was not yet established in the cave, for Esau was disputing it. Therefore I buried her on the road. But when I buried Leah, Esau had already gone to his land and left me everything." "<b>And I buried her there.</b> For I knew that that territory would rise as the portion of her son, and it is an honor for her to be buried in her son's portion. And so it says, and you find there two men at Rachel's burial, in the territory of Benjamin, in Tzelzach. And had I buried her in the cave, it would not be her honor, for it is in the portion of Judah, son of Leah. Another interpretation: therefore Jacob buried her there, because it is disgraceful for a woman who died in childbirth to be taken far and kept waiting, lest her blood soil her shrouds. And since he wanted to be buried in the land of Canaan, he mentioned this to Joseph, so that he would not blame him concerning his mother and would not be negligent in the matter. This is the reading according to Rashi, for Rachel's burial is indeed in the land of Israel."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {1 "The abbreviation חז״ק is resolved here as 'חזי״ן קרי' (this is the reading), introducing a clarification of the preceding statement in relation to Rashi's reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:03.754133238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}